cards.text:
Think about the last time you felt genuinely bad about yourself. What triggered it?

{red|Was it a social media scroll? A comparison to someone else? A perceived failure? Being single at an event?}

Trace the feeling back to the lie it connects to.

{red|When something goes wrong, a rejection, a failure, a disappointment, what does your inner voice typically say?}

This reveals what your identity is actually built on. If rejection makes you feel worthless, your identity might be built on others' acceptance. If failure devastates you, it might be built on achievement.

{red|What does your reaction to difficulty reveal about your foundation?}

Think about your self-talk over the past few days. What does your inner voice typically say to you?

{red|Is it kind? Critical? Harsh? Encouraging? Shaming?}

Write down some of the phrases you most commonly hear in your head about yourself.

{red|Where do your boundaries tend to be weakest?}

With family? At work? In dating? With friends?

{red|What makes it hard for you to set or maintain boundaries in those areas?}

Think about the people you've been attracted to or dated. What patterns do you notice?

{red|Are there common traits, positive or negative, that keep showing up?}

{red|How might these patterns connect to your own identity wounds or beliefs about yourself?}
